WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.069
The Incredibles are back with a brand new
teaser trailer for the super-long-awaited

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:06.069
sequel!

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:09.680
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to break down

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:18.160
the new teaser for Pixar's Incredibles 2.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.350
I'm really excited for this movie; I love
the style of the animation and the score by

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.320
Michael Giacchino is just gorgeous, so I can't
wait to see and hear lots more of that!

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.550
The way the teaser kicks off will feel familiar
to you if you've watched Pixar's short film

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.530
Jack-Jack Attack, where you'll have seen the
Parr Family's youngest child pass through

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.510
solid objects like he does here.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:47.980
Notice in the teaser footage that when Jack-Jack
uses his laser vision, it's green, whereas

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.719
in Jack-Jack Attack, it's actually purple.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:56.192
I wonder if there's a significant reason behind
that change of colour, or whether it's that

00:00:56.192 --> 00:01:01.120
the filmmakers think this new colour looks
better with the rest of the new movie, or,

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.940
perhaps most likely, it's just because the
background in this teaser is red and Jack-Jack's

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.440
laser vision wouldn't have stood out as clearly
against that if it had been purple instead

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.200
of the green colour they've gone for here.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.620
I thought it was really fun the way they use
Jack-Jack to create the movie's new logo from

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.620
the old one.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.360
So we see Jack-Jack using his Laser Vision
to split the single 'i' to create two 'i's,

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:27.100
which is a really cool and clever way to show
visually that this is the second film, Incredibles

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.100
2.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.770
And it was also funny later in the clip when
he zaps his dad, splitting his hair in two

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.320
down the middle in a similar way.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.600
We already saw Jack-Jack unleash a variety
of superpowers in front of his babysitter

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.390
and against the villainous Syndrome in both
the first Incredibles feature film and the

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.390
short film.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:48.671
But his parents didn't see those powers because
when Syndrome was battling the baby high up

00:01:48.671 --> 00:01:51.960
in the sky, Jack-Jack's family were on the
ground below.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.760
However, at the very end of The Incredibles,
we did see Jack-Jack don a mask, like the

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.050
rest of his family, seemingly ready to do
battle with the villain The Underminer, who

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:04.590
was voiced by Pixar's good-luck-charm, John
Ratzenberger.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.470
And that's exactly where the new movie will
pick up too.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.850
"Behold the Underminer!"

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:16.870
"I hereby declare war on peace and happiness!"

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.420
Some Incredibles 2 footage that screened at
D23 this summer showed Jack-Jack using his

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:25.569
powers against a raccoon, and his father Bob
waking up and cheering 'He has powers'.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:29.860
And if you compare that to this new teaser
trailer, it sounds a little like this is a

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:33.079
variation of the end of that D23 footage.

00:02:33.079 --> 00:02:35.870
"You have powers!"

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.730
"Yeah, baby!"

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:42.560
I love the way in this teaser that his father
is so proud of his son's superhero abilities.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.530
And I also love the way that Jack-Jack seems
to sneeze here which causes him to course

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:51.970
through a range of his powers in a similar
way to how he seemed to hiccup in Jack-Jack

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:56.849
Attack just before he turned into a fire-ball,
showing perhaps that he's not in complete

00:02:56.849 --> 00:03:00.709
control yet of all his powers!

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:03.319
"Hic!"

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:06.959
It's a shame we don't get to see the whole
family in the teaser, though I'm sure we'll

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:09.279
see more of them in the first full trailer.

00:03:09.279 --> 00:03:14.019
According to writer-director Brad Bird, Elastigirl
will be at the forefront of the action in

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:20.340
the new feature, while Bob Parr, aka Mr Incredible,
'has to stay home facing his biggest challenge

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.049
yet', and I'm guessing that some of that challenge
will be linked to what we've just seen in

00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:27.309
this teaser and the revelation of Jack-Jack's
superpowers.

00:03:27.309 --> 00:03:30.450
So, how excited are you for Incredibles 2?

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.450
And what did you think of the teaser trailer?

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.439
Let me know in the comments below.

00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:39.840
Make sure you subscribe and turn on notifications
to get all my new Disney and Pixar videos,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.220
including Pixar's Coco later this week.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.549
And tap the screen right here for more videos
I'm sure you'll enjoy!

00:03:45.549 --> 00:03:47.730
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:48.749
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

